{
  "_README": [
    "IMPORTANT, PLEASE READ BEFORE TRUSTING THE 'native %' NUMBERS.",
    "",
    "The columns this project reads from the PMC Tree Census 2019 are: geom,",
    "girth_cm, height_m, condition, ownership, ward, botanical_name,",
    "common_name, local_name, economic_i, flowering, is_rare (required), plus",
    "ward_name, canopy_dia_m, phenology, id, sr_no and road_name if present.",
    "None of them says where a species came from.",
    "",
    "The full header as actually published is recorded in public/data/meta.json",
    "under source.header_seen on every build -- read that, not this file, if you",
    "want the authoritative column list.",
    "",
    "So the nativity shown on this site is NOT census data. It is a curated",
    "reference list of botanical origin, maintained here in the open, mapping",
    "botanical name -> 'native' (indigenous to the Indian subcontinent) or",
    "'non_native' (introduced from elsewhere, however long ago).",
    "",
    "Any species NOT in this list is reported as 'unknown' and is counted",
    "separately. It is never silently bucketed as native or non-native.",
    "",
    "'Native' here means indigenous to the Indian subcontinent, not endemic to",
    "the Western Ghats or to Maharashtra specifically. Botanists disagree at the",
    "edges (Tamarindus indica and Cocos nucifera are the classic arguments).",
    "Corrections are welcome as a pull request against this file."
  ],
